IMPORT prelude

-- Singapore Sports Council Act 1973 (Singapore) -- what counts as "sports" (s 2), the scope of the Council's functions (s 8),
-- membership and the Chairperson (ss 4, 4A), meetings, quorum and the casting vote (s 6), fees for facilities (s 9(g)),
-- borrowing (s 20), payments to members (ss 5, 21(2)), protection for bona fide acts (s 23), and the financial year and the
-- audited-statements deadline (Schedule paras 1 and 4).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to 1 December 2021, in operation 31 December 2021), informal
-- consolidation "version in force from 1/4/2026", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SSCA1973.txt. The latest
-- amendment annotated is Act 4 of 2026 with effect from 1 April 2026 (it added "mind sport" and widened "sports", among
-- others). The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is out of step with the body for Part 5 (it lists ss 14-16
-- as repealed; the body has ss 14 and 15 in force and ss 16-18 repealed). This encoding follows the body.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0215 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. The honest answer is: very little directly. This is a constitutive Act for a statutory board. A
-- person meets it as a player of a "sport" (now including chess, bridge and e-sports), a user of a Council facility paying
-- a fee, a member of the Council, a lender, or someone harmed by a Council employee's act.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the transfer of undertakings and staff in 1973 (ss 11-13), the Chief Executive Officer and staff (ss 14, 15),
-- the Minister's directions (s 10), the Council's general powers beyond fees and loans (s 9), shares to the Minister for
-- Finance (s 20A), investment (s 21(3)), regulations (s 24), and the budget (Schedule paras 2, 3). No regulations made under
-- s 24 (for example on use of the National Stadium) were retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Singapore Sports Council Act 1973`

§§ `2 and 8 -- what counts as sports, and what the Council is for`

-- s 2: "'mind sport' means a competitive game based on intellectual skill rather than physical skill, such as chess or
-- bridge"; "'sports' includes mind sports and e-sports" [Act 4 of 2026 wef 01/04/2026]. "e-sports" is NOT defined.
-- "includes" extends the ordinary meaning, so physical sport stays within it (an inference from the word "includes").
-- s 8(a): "to plan and promote sports and physical fitness activities in Singapore for both competitive and recreational
-- purposes"; (e): physical education.
DECLARE Activity
    HAS `is a physical sport` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is a game of intellectual rather than physical skill` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is competitive` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is an e-sport` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is a physical fitness activity` IS A BOOLEAN
        `is physical education` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a mind sport` IF
    `the activity`'s `is a game of intellectual rather than physical skill` AND `the activity`'s `is competitive`

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is sports` IF
        `the activity`'s `is a physical sport`
    OR  `is a mind sport` `the activity`
    OR  `the activity`'s `is an e-sport`

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is within the Council's promotional functions` IF
        `is sports` `the activity`
    OR  `the activity`'s `is a physical fitness activity`
    OR  `the activity`'s `is physical education`

§§ `4 -- membership`

-- s 4(1): "not less than 7 and not more than 25 members, each of whom is to be appointed by the Minister" [Act 4 of 2026].
-- (3): "holds office for a period of 3 years, or for such shorter period as the Minister may determine, and is eligible for
-- re-appointment". (5): a replacement serves "for the unexpired period of the term of office" of the member replaced.
-- (6): "No vacancy in the membership of the Council affects its powers."
GIVEN `number of members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Council's size is within the Act` IF
    `number of members` AT LEAST 7 AND `number of members` AT MOST 25

GIVEN `term in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a member's term is within the Act` IF
    `term in months` GREATER THAN 0 AND `term in months` AT MOST 36

GIVEN `predecessor's term in months` IS A NUMBER, `months the predecessor served` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the replacement's term in months` MEANS
    IF `months the predecessor served` AT LEAST `predecessor's term in months` THEN 0
    ELSE `predecessor's term in months` MINUS `months the predecessor served`

§§ `4(2) and 4A -- Chairperson and Deputy Chairperson`

-- s 4(2): "One of the members (who is not the Chairperson) may be the Chief Executive Officer."
-- s 4A(1): the Minister may appoint (a) "a member (other than the Chief Executive Officer)" as Chairperson and (b) "a member
-- (other than the Chairperson or Chief Executive Officer)" as Deputy Chairperson, each "for a period the Minister
-- determines, being not longer than 3 years". (3): office ends at the first of (a) expiry of the term, (b) ceasing to be a
-- member, (c) revocation by the Minister.
GIVEN `is a member` IS A BOOLEAN, `is the Chief Executive Officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `term in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be appointed Chairperson` IF
    `is a member` AND (NOT `is the Chief Executive Officer`) AND `term in months` GREATER THAN 0 AND `term in months` AT MOST 36

GIVEN `is a member` IS A BOOLEAN, `is the Chief Executive Officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `is the Chairperson` IS A BOOLEAN, `term in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be appointed Deputy Chairperson` IF
        `is a member` AND (NOT `is the Chief Executive Officer`) AND (NOT `is the Chairperson`)
    AND `term in months` GREATER THAN 0 AND `term in months` AT MOST 36

GIVEN `term has expired` IS A BOOLEAN, `still a member` IS A BOOLEAN, `appointment revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `still holds office as Chairperson` IF
    (NOT `term has expired`) AND `still a member` AND (NOT `appointment revoked`)

§§ `6 -- meetings, quorum, who presides, and the casting vote`

-- s 6(2): "5 members or half of the total number of members of the Council (whichever is the higher) constitute a quorum"
-- [Act 4 of 2026]. Read here as: at least 5 present AND at least half of the total present. With an odd total, half is not
-- a whole number; "at least half" means rounding up (an inference; the text does not say).
-- (3): the Chairperson presides if present, otherwise the Deputy Chairperson; (4): if both are absent, "the members present
-- must elect one of their number to preside".
-- (5): "decided by a majority of the votes of the members present", and on an equality "the Chairperson or the member
-- presiding at the meeting has a casting vote in addition to his or her original vote".
GIVEN `total members` IS A NUMBER, `members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a quorum` IF
    `members present` AT LEAST 5 AND `members present` TIMES 2 AT LEAST `total members`

DECLARE Presider IS ONE OF
    `the Chairperson`
    `the Deputy Chairperson`
    `a member elected by those present`

GIVEN `Chairperson present` IS A BOOLEAN, `Deputy present` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Presider
`who presides` MEANS
    IF `Chairperson present` THEN `the Chairperson`
    ELSE IF `Deputy present` THEN `the Deputy Chairperson`
         ELSE `a member elected by those present`

-- The presider's original vote is counted in `votes for` or `votes against`; the casting vote is extra.
GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `presider casts the casting vote for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the question is carried` IF
        `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against`
    OR  (`votes for` EQUALS `votes against` AND `presider casts the casting vote for`)

§§ `9(g) -- fees for services and facilities`

-- s 9(g): the Council may, "with the approval of the Minister -- (i) impose fees or charges for services rendered by the
-- Council and for the use of any facilities controlled or managed by the Council; and (ii) determine the amount of each
-- such fee or charge". The approval runs to both the fee and its amount.
GIVEN `Minister approved imposing the fee` IS A BOOLEAN, `Minister approved the amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Council may charge the fee` IF
    `Minister approved imposing the fee` AND `Minister approved the amount`

§§ `20 -- borrowing`

-- s 20(1): loans (a) "from the Government"; (b) "with the approval in writing of the Minister, from any person", with power to
-- mortgage, charge or pledge its property; (c) "with the approval in writing of the Minister, by the creation and issue of
-- debentures or bonds". (2): an overdraft or other temporary borrowing (a) to defray expenses "pending the receipt of
-- revenues" for that period of account, or (b) pending money due on a loan raised under (1). No ministerial approval is
-- written into (2).
DECLARE Borrowing IS ONE OF
    `a loan from the Government`
    `a loan from a bank or other person`
    `an issue of bonds or debentures`
    `a temporary overdraft pending revenue`
    `a temporary overdraft pending a loan`
    `a temporary overdraft for some other purpose`

GIVEN `the borrowing` IS A Borrowing, `Minister's written approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Council may borrow` IF
    CONSIDER `the borrowing`
    WHEN `a loan from the Government` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a loan from a bank or other person` THEN `Minister's written approval`
    WHEN `an issue of bonds or debentures` THEN `Minister's written approval`
    WHEN `a temporary overdraft pending revenue` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a temporary overdraft pending a loan` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a temporary overdraft for some other purpose` THEN FALSE

§§ `5 and 21(2) -- what a member may be paid`

-- s 5: members are paid "such salaries, fees and allowances as the Minister may determine". s 21(2): "no portion thereof may
-- be paid or transferred directly or indirectly by way of dividend, bonus or otherwise by way of profit to its members".
DECLARE PaymentToMember IS ONE OF
    `a salary, fee or allowance the Minister determined`
    `a salary, fee or allowance the Minister did not determine`
    `a dividend`
    `a profit-sharing bonus`

GIVEN `the payment` IS A PaymentToMember
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment to a member is permitted` IF
    CONSIDER `the payment`
    WHEN `a salary, fee or allowance the Minister determined` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `23 -- protection from liability for bona fide acts`

-- s 23: no matter or thing done and no contract entered into by the Council, and no matter or thing done by any member or
-- employee, "shall, if the matter or thing was done or the contract was entered into bona fide for the purpose of carrying
-- out the provisions of this Act, subject any such member or employee to any action, liability, claim or demand".
-- The protection is for members and employees personally. The section does not say the COUNCIL is protected.
DECLARE Defendant IS ONE OF
    `the Council itself`
    `a member`
    `an employee`

GIVEN `who is sued` IS A Defendant, `done bona fide` IS A BOOLEAN, `done to carry out the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 23 bars the claim` IF
    CONSIDER `who is sued`
    WHEN `the Council itself` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `done bona fide` AND `done to carry out the Act`

§§ `Schedule paras 1 and 4 -- financial year and audited statements`

-- Para 1: "The financial year of the Council begins on 1 April of each year and ends on 31 March of the succeeding year."
-- Para 4: the audited annual financial statements, "signed by the Chairperson and the Chief Executive Officer", go to the
-- Minister "no later than 31 October in each year", with any auditor's report.
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER, `month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the financial year starting in` MEANS
    IF `month` AT LEAST 4 THEN `year` ELSE `year` MINUS 1

GIVEN `month sent` IS A NUMBER, `signed by Chairperson` IS A BOOLEAN, `signed by CEO` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the audited statements comply` IF
    `month sent` AT MOST 10 AND `signed by Chairperson` AND `signed by CEO`
